Subject: [PATCH 2/2] sunxi: rg35xx-2024: keep the DRAM voltage the SPL set

U-Boot proper set vdd-dram back to the device tree's fixed 1.1V when the
AXP717's regulators probed, as the regulator uclass does for an
always-on regulator whose minimum equals its maximum. With
SUNXI_DRAM_H616_LPDDR4_OR_LPDDR3 the SPL sets 1.2V for LPDDR3, which
this undid; Linux, given the same range, then kept the 1.1V. A range of
1.1V to 1.2V in U-Boot's copy of the device tree leaves the voltage
where the SPL set it.
---
 .../sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-2024-u-boot.dtsi   | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/dts/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-2024-u-boot.dtsi

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-2024-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-2024-u-boot.dtsi
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..51e59088
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-2024-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0+ OR MIT)
+
+#include "sunxi-u-boot.dtsi"
+
+/*
+ * Every Anbernic H700 board builds U-Boot with this device tree, but they come
+ * with LPDDR4 (1.1V) or LPDDR3 (1.2V), and the SPL sets the voltage for the one
+ * it finds. With min equal to max, the regulator uclass would set 1.1V again
+ * when the PMIC's regulators probe, undervolting LPDDR3; a range leaves it be.
+ */
+&reg_dcdc3 {
+	regulator-min-microvolt = <1100000>;
+	regulator-max-microvolt = <1200000>;
+};
